        "original_id": "9e8eb791-0eab-5020-83e4-b8725611bad1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Eric Musselman, Bill Musselman, Chuck Daly, Doc Rivers, Lon Kruger, Yanni Hufnagel\n- Organizations: Minnesota Timberwolves, Orlando Magic, Atlanta Hawks, Detroit Pistons, Nevada Wolf Pack men's basketball team, United States men's Olympic basketball team\n- Roles: head coaches, assistant coaches\n- Leagues and Events: Continental Basketball Association, National Basketball Association, 1992 Summer Olympics\n\nFacts:\n- Chuck Daly was an American basketball head coach born on July 20, 1930, and he died on May 9, 2009.\n- Chuck Daly led the Detroit Pistons to consecutive NBA championships in 1989 and 1990.\n- Chuck Daly coached the 1992 United States men's Olympic basketball team, known as the Dream Team, to a gold medal at the 1992 Summer Olympics.\n- Eric Musselman is the son of former NBA head coach Bill Musselman.\n- Eric Musselman was a head coach in the Continental Basketball Association before becoming an assistant coach in the NBA.\n- Eric Musselman served as an assistant coach with the Minnesota Timberwolves, the Orlando Magic under Chuck Daly and Doc Rivers, and the Atlanta Hawks under Lon Kruger.\n- Yanni Hufnagel last served as an assistant coach for the Nevada Wolf Pack men's basketball team under Eric Musselman.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "4db95944-4fea-5fa5-a2ba-9333b977a9c0",
        "text": "Page: Eric Musselman. Sentence: The son of former NBA head coach Bill Musselman, Eric Musselman was a head coach in the Continental Basketball Association (CBA) before becoming an assistant coach with the Minnesota Timberwolves, Orlando Magic (under Chuck Daly and Doc Rivers), and Atlanta Hawks (under Lon Kruger).\nPage: Chuck Daly. Sentence: Charles Jerome Daly (July 20, 1930 – May 9, 2009) was an American basketball head coach.\nPage: Chuck Daly. Sentence: He led the Detroit Pistons to consecutive National Basketball Association (NBA) Championships in 1989 and 1990, and the 1992 United States men's Olympic basketball team (\"The Dream Team\") to the gold medal at the 1992 Summer Olympics.\nPage: Yanni Hufnagel. Sentence: He last served as an assistant coach of the Nevada Wolf Pack men's basketball team under Eric Musselman.",
